#Installation
1. Clone the repo
2. cd into the repo (`cd lanchatty`)
3. `python -m venv .venv`
4. `source .venv/bin/activate`
5. `pip install -r requirements.txt`

#Usage
>Both users must be connected to the same network
1. Assuming already inside repo directory, `cd src`
2. User 1 runs `python main.py --serve`
3. User 2 runs `python main.py --join --ip <User 1's local IP address>`
4. Profit
